=====================================================================
(2) THE EXIT STATUS IS NOT SWALLOWED -- PASS
=====================================================================
Static: the four added lines carry no `-` prefix, no `|| true`, no `||` at all,
and no pipeline.
  $ awk 'NR>=185 && NR<=230' Makefile | grep -nE '^\t-|\|\| *true|\|\|'
    -> the ONLY hit is line 210 inside `fuzz`: `... || exit $$?`, which
       PROPAGATES status rather than swallowing it. None of the added lines.
  $ grep -nE '^\.IGNORE|MAKEFLAGS|\.SHELLFLAGS|^SHELL|\.ONESHELL' Makefile
    -> rc 1, no matches. No global error suppression, no -k baked in, no
       .ONESHELL that could merge the two commands into one shell whose exit
       status is the last one only.
Behavioural (stronger, and the one I rely on): six `make: *** [Makefile:NNN:
target] Error 1` lines above, each naming the added line, with shell rc 2. If
the status were swallowed the target would have exited 0, as the attempt-7
control does.
Ordering: in test-coverage the added line precedes `go tool cover`, so a failure
aborts before the report is regenerated -- confirmed, coverage.html kept its
pre-run mtime (Jul 4 13:52) after `make test-coverage` failed.

